## Model card (verified facts only — no scores)

- **Name:** Fledge Alpha (`fledge-alpha` / `opencode/fledge-alpha` / `opencode/fledge-alpha-free`); also referenced as `Fledge Alpha Free`. Listed in OpenCode Zen free tier (released 2026-10-01, removed/deprecated by 2026-10-08 per `stealthmodels.com`). Not labeled as a stealth model in the OpenCode catalog (unlike Space Bunny / Big Pickle) — explicit naming by provider.
- **Short description:** A free preview/reasoning model offered through OpenCode Zen. Listed specs: 1,048,576 token context, 131,072 max output, text + image input, text output, reasoning (low/high/max), tool-calling supported, $0.00 pricing. Identity unconfirmed: fingerprint analysis (`lm.ikale.io`) points to Claude Opus 5.5 (99.4%); alternative fingerprint theories (`linkedin.com`) point to Thinking Machines Lab / Inkling (Tinker serverless settings, 262K serverless route, 32,800 output cap in first PR version, effort levels mapped to Inkling presets 0.2/0.9/0.99, image encoding 40px patches); OpenCode's own AI agent wrote the catalog entry and referenced Tinker settings, then edited out the reference. No official vendor identity confirmed by OpenCode, Thinking Machines Lab, Anthropic, or any provider. No official benchmark card published.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode (`opencode.ai` / `zen/v1/models`) — free endpoint only (`opencode` host, $0/$0 per `models.dev`); not on OpenRouter (no verified `openrouter.ai` benchmark/price entry for `fledge-alpha` in fetched sources); not on Amazon Bedrock, Cloudflare AI, or NVIDIA NIM. Access restricted by geography (European users report unavailability per `linkedin.com` / `freeaiapi.org`). Not an open-weights release (`open_weights = false` per `models.dev`).
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-10-01 (OpenCode catalog addition via PR; `models.dev` release date 2026-10-01; `freeaiapi.org` review 2026-10-07); deprecated/retired by 2026-10-08 (`stealthmodels.com` — "Fledge Alpha is no longer available through OpenCode Zen"); `models.dev` TOML `status = "deprecated"`. Knowledge cutoff not stated; no official model card or documentation beyond spec TOML and third-party reviews.
- **IDs:** `fledge-alpha` (primary); `opencode/fledge-alpha` (provider/model route); `opencode/fledge-alpha-free` (free tier variant per `freeaiapi.org`); `x-preview-f-free` (OpenRouter stealth route mentioned in `linkedin.com` but not verified in fetched `openrouter.ai` results). No separate ID for reasoning levels (low/high/max mapped to internal numeric values, not model IDs).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens (1M) — verified by `models.dev` TOML (`context = 1_048_576`), `allaimodel.com`, `custom.typingmind.com`, `freeaiapi.org`, `stealthmodels.com` — full agreement. Max output: 131,072 tokens (`models.dev` TOML `output = 131_072`; `freeaiapi.org`; `stealthmodels.com`). Note: initial PR version (`models.dev` edit history per `linkedin.com`) listed 262,144 context / 32,800 output / audio input / 6 effort levels (`none`, `minimal`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`) — replaced 2 minutes 46 seconds later with current 1M/131K spec; no audio in final spec (`models.dev` TOML input only `text`, `image`). The initial spec may reflect a different serving route or a pre-release configuration (potentially linked to Tinker/Inkling specs), not the final `exo-free` endpoint.
- **Modalities:** Input: text + image (`models.dev` TOML: `input = ["text", "image"]`; `freeaiapi.org` confirms image/video input per OpenRouter profile but final `models.dev` excludes video; closest verified is text + image). Output: text only (`output = ["text"]`). Reasoning: yes — `reasoning = { supported = true, effort = ["high"] }` (`models.dev` TOML notes `reasoning_effort = high (deprecated; not re-verified on Zen)` — indicates reasoning support exists but may not be actively verified/re-tested). Tool calling: yes (`tools = { supported = true }`). Temperature control: no (`temperature = false` — fixed temperature). Structured outputs / JSON mode: not explicitly confirmed in fetched sources; closest proxy is agentic/reasoning capability claim.
- **Pricing:** $0.00 input / $0.00 output per 1M tokens (`models.dev` TOML; `allaimodel.com`; `custom.typingmind.com`; `freeaiapi.org` — full agreement). Free route; no commercial pricing tier. Cost efficiency is maximum (free tokens) but only if benchmarks/performance justify usage — no verified performance evidence exists.
- **Architecture:** Not disclosed (`models.dev` TOML does not list parameters, MoE/dense, layer count, weights, or architecture). Fingerprinting evidence: `lm.ikale.io` 99.4% Claude Opus 5.5 (token-generation bias); `linkedin.com` / `freeaiapi.org` note potential Thinking Machines Lab / Inkling connection (Tinker serverless settings, 262K/32,800 initial PR spec matching Inkling specs, 40px image patches, 0.2/0.9/0.99 effort levels mapping to Inkling presets, Chinese backend errors, GLM-family token patterns). Not open-weights; no public weights; proprietary/free-route model.

### Raw benchmarks found (independent public verification — ZERO FOUND for exact ID `exo-free`)

Sources checked (3+ independent categories):
1. **Official provider / spec documentation** (`models.dev` TOML / `allaimodel.com` / `opencode.ai` spec docs / `freeaiapi.org`) — confirms specs, deprecated status, $0 pricing, identity ambiguity, no benchmark scores. The `models.dev` TOML explicitly references external benchmark sources (`Epoch AI`, `SWE-bench`, `LiveBench`, `Aider`) in its benchmark-section header but does not list any verified scores for `exo-free` in the fetched content.
2. **Independent benchmark registries / aggregators** (`benchmarkregistry.org`, `benchgap.net`, `artificialanalysis.ai`, `modelbenchmark.io`) — no entry or verified score found specifically for `exo-free` / `opencode/exo-free`. `modelbenchmark.io` lists `exo-free` with specs (1M context, 131K output, $0/$0) but no verified benchmark numbers (benchmark section references external sources without listing scores). `benchmarklist.com` does not include `exo-free` in the fetched results.
3. **Independent review / analysis / fingerprinting sources** (`linkedin.com` / `freeaiapi.org` / `stealthmodels.com` / `fellipesoares.com.br`) — focus on fingerprint identity, privacy/data-retention warnings, endpoint volatility (429/dropouts), small non-representative DeepSWE subset, community smoke tests (3D Blender, vision, script execution) — none provide verified standard benchmark scores. The `fellipesoares.com.br` comparison (15/15 custom harness runs) and `linkedin.com` DeepSWE subset (10/113 tasks, 80%) are explicitly non-representative and high-variance; the `freeaiapi.org` review notes fingerprinting confidence but also discusses economic/privacy implications rather than benchmark verification.

Conflict comparison (relevant — all relate to absence of evidence rather than conflicting numbers):
- **Identity / provider:** `lm.ikale.io` fingerprint 99.4% Claude Opus 5.5 vs potential Thinking Machines Lab / Inkling connection (Tinker settings, initial PR spec matching Inkling, 40px patches) vs GLM-family fingerprint patterns (`linkedin.com` / `freeaiapi.org`) vs synthetic-output/distillation theory (`freeaiapi.org`). No verified identity confirmation from any official provider; OpenCode has not named the model's origin. This identity ambiguity does not directly affect benchmark scores (since none exist) but explains why no official benchmark card is available.
- **DeepSWE subset:** Official/vendor benchmark: none published for `exo-free`. Independent small subset (`linkedin.com`): 80% on 10/113 tasks (explicitly caveated as non-representative, high variance, cannot establish leaderboard ranking). Independent comparison (`fellipesoares.com.br`): 15/15 custom harness runs (not a standard benchmark; cost comparison uses DeepSeek V4.1 Flash pricing proxy because the free route has no commercial price). **No numerical conflict — only absence of full-dataset verified scores.**
- **Performance / capability:** Community smoke tests (`freeaiapi.org` — 3D Blender rendering, vision understanding, script generation) confirm basic capability but are not standardized benchmarks. No verified SWE-bench Verified, SWE-bench Pro, LiveCodeBench v6, AIME, GPQA Diamond, MMLU-Pro, HLE, Terminal-Bench, SciCode, AA Intelligence Index, or equivalent scores found for exact ID `exo-free`. The closest verified benchmark reference in `models.dev` TOML points to external sources (`SWE-bench`, `LiveBench`, `Aider`, `Epoch AI`) but does not list any extracted score for this model.
- **Status / availability:** `models.dev` TOML `status = "deprecated"` (release 2026-10-06) vs endpoint still listed/accessible (`opencode.ai` / `linkedin.com` / `freeaiapi.org` as of 2026-10-07/2026-10-29). The `models.dev` deprecated status may refer to the specific route/config rather than complete removal (the endpoint continues to be referenced in reviews). No conflict affects benchmark verification — both confirm the model exists but lacks verified scores.
- **Privacy / data use:** `models.dev` TOML does not list a zero-retention policy; `freeaiapi.org` explicitly notes no zero-data-retention guarantee, user data retained for future model training; `linkedin.com` notes OpenCode's privacy section states data may be used to improve the model; `freeaiapi.org` compares this to Space Bunny (zero retention) and Muse Spark Contributor (training on prompts for discount). This is a verified usage-policy difference, not a benchmark conflict.

Agent / tool use / reasoning / coding / multimodal / long context / cost efficiency:
- **Every category:** `no verified public score found` for exact model ID `exo-free`. The closest non-benchmark capability confirmations are spec-level only: tool-calling yes (`models.dev`); reasoning yes (`models.dev`, `reasoning_effort = high` deprecated); context 1M verified; image input yes (`models.dev`); text output only (`models.dev`); $0 price verified; deprecated status verified. No verified agentic/autonomous benchmark (SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, DeepSWE full set, APEX-Agents, AutomationBench, Tau2-Bench, MCP Atlas, Claw-Eval, etc.) found specifically for this exact ID.
